      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define shared storage, stacking rules, and tool usage process.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 237414,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Alright everyone, I've put together a first draft of the shared tool and storage rules in A3, based on my task T3. It covers labelling, designated areas for each team's common items, and a checkout system for shared power tools. Please review and add your comments.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 11765,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "I looked at A3. Where do I put my precision tools and components? I can't have them in a dusty cabinet with the big hammers.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 54659,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "This looks like a good start. Two things from my side: 1) We need a designated area for items that can be wet or dirty, like shovels and hoses, separate from dry storage. 2) What about bulk items like bags of fertilizer or soil? They take up floor space but aren't heavy. The doc mainly talks about shelving.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 237414,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Good catch, @11765. Your clean zone should have its own dedicated, sealed storage cabinets. I'll add a section in A3 for 'Zone-Specific Storage' to make that clear.",
            "mentions": [
              11765
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 237414,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Both valid points, @54659. I'll add a 'Wet/Dirty Tool Rack' section and a 'Bulk Floor Storage' area with clear floor markings. I've updated A3 with these changes.",
            "mentions": [
              54659
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 149461,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "So we have to sign out every drill?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 237414,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "Just the high-power ones that are shared across teams, like the hammer drill and concrete saw. Standard hand tools for your zone will have their own place. It's all in A3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 21079,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "The storage plan in A3 is fine, but it's missing the stacking and loading rules from T7. We need to be explicit about max pallet heights in the staging area, especially under the crane path. I propose a max height of 1.5 meters for any stack in the main corridor. Also, all heavy materials must be stored on the ground level of racks, never higher.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "warning",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 54659,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "That makes sense. We should also specify that nothing can be stacked in the garden access path, even temporarily.",
